From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: fork through the host

A fork child needs its parent's call stack, which lives in the host's
WebAssembly engine, not in memory the kernel can copy: clone(SIGCHLD)
gave the child an empty address space and no stack, and it died on its
first instruction. _Fork now asks the host (__gmux_fork), which captures
the parent's frames, forks the task through the kernel, gives the child a
copy of the parent's memory and resumes the frames in both. It returns
the child's pid to the parent and 0 to the child, or -ENOSYS for a
program built without resumable frames.
---
--- a/src/process/_Fork.c
+++ b/src/process/_Fork.c
@@ -26,15 +26,21 @@
 	if (!ret) __aio_atfork(1);
 }
 
+#ifdef __wasm__
+long __gmux_fork(void);
+#endif
+
 pid_t _Fork(void)
 {
 	pid_t ret;
 	sigset_t set;
 	__block_all_sigs(&set);
 	LOCK(__abort_lock);
-#ifdef SYS_fork
+#if defined(__wasm__)
+	ret = __gmux_fork();
+#elif defined(SYS_fork)
 	ret = __syscall(SYS_fork);
 #else
 	ret = __syscall(SYS_clone, SIGCHLD, 0);
 #endif
 	__post_Fork(ret);
